# Research brief

## Frozen objective (experiment-repo issue #1)

> Estimate π by Monte Carlo sampling.
>
> Draw 1,000,000 points uniformly in the unit square, count those inside the quarter circle of radius 1, and take 4 × (inside / total) as the estimate. Repeat with 20 independent seeds and report the mean estimate with a 95% confidence interval across the seeds, and its error against math.pi.
>
> Report: `report/report.md`, half a page: the estimate, the interval, the error and how many points were drawn in all.

## Supplied material and interpretation

The complete issue contains the objective above; no data files, related papers, or other input material are supplied. The data must be generated by the requested Monte Carlo experiment. No literature comparison or figure is required.

Sample independent pseudorandom uniform coordinate pairs (x,y) in [0,1)² and count x²+y² ≤ 1. Each of 20 independent seeded streams supplies 1,000,000 points. Retain every seed identifier, count and estimate. The required total is 20,000,000 study points. Use the arithmetic mean of the 20 estimates and a two-sided Student t interval with 19 degrees of freedom, using the sample standard deviation across seeds divided by √20. This is an approximate confidence interval based on independent replicate means. Report signed error (mean minus math.pi) and absolute error to remove ambiguity in “error.”

## Work and checks

Experiment owns context, assignment, reproducible sampling, numerical results and diagnostics. Paper owns the half-page final Markdown report. Internal review independently checks the methods, counts, uncertainty and final report. Check equal replicate sizes, exactly 20 distinct streams, count-to-estimate arithmetic, total draws and interval arithmetic. Compare observed seed variability with the known Bernoulli variance as a diagnostic, without altering seeds or sample size according to the result. A timed pilot, if used for execution sizing, is separate from the 20 study replicates and its draws will be disclosed separately.

## Unestablished points

No seed convention or interval formula is stipulated. The choices above will be fixed before sampling and recorded with software versions. The completed results are in results/summary.json and results/per_seed.csv; results/validation.md records checks and interpretation. All requested study draws are complete. No additional pilot draws were made.
